        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Nationality adjectives",
          "text": "They agree with the person. Common feminine endings:\n- -ien → -ienne (italien / italienne), -ain → -aine (marocain / marocaine), -ais → -aise (français / française), -ois → -oise (chinois / chinoise), -ol → -ole (espagnol / espagnole), or simply + e (allemand / allemande).\n- Adjectives already ending in -e don't change: belge, russe, suisse.\n- Small letter for the adjective (Elle est indienne), capital letter for the person (une Indienne).\n- In the feminine the final consonant is pronounced: indien /ɛ̃djɛ̃/ vs indienne /ɛ̃djɛn/, allemand vs allemande.\n- Gotcha: the country has an article (la France) but after habiter it becomes en France, au Canada (see Leçon 12)."
        },
